# Line endings are pinned, not left to whoever clones this.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is a per-machine setting, so without this file the same commit checks out
# differently on two developers's disks and the difference shows up as a diff nobody made.
# orbistoun and obSCEne both learned this the hard way and carry their own; this is the same
# rule for the meta-repository. See OOPS conventions section 8.
#
# `text=auto` rather than a list of extensions: git detects binary content itself, and a list
# only protects the extensions somebody remembered.
* text=auto eol=lf
